{
  "title": "Interaural audiogram-shape mismatch does not establish added HbA1c prediction across two NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "Among 3,636 source and 4,056 target complete-case adults, offset-free interaural audiogram-shape mismatch did not establish incremental HbA1c prediction beyond BMI, demographics, bilateral hearing levels and conventional asymmetry: target augmented-minus-baseline MSE -0.000012877 squared HbA1c percentage points; joint source-refit/target PSU-bootstrap 95% interval [-0.000564291, 0.001650151]. This is exploratory independent-participant cross-cycle transfer, not equivalence or independent-site validation.",
  "keywords": [
    "audiometry",
    "HbA1c",
    "interaural asymmetry",
    "NHANES",
    "negative result",
    "cross-cycle prediction"
  ],
